  "id": "implicit-leadership-theories",
  "term": "implicit leadership theories",
  "definition": "Implicit leadership theories are the mental templates people hold about what traits and behaviors a leader should have. People use these internal prototypes to judge whether someone fits their idea of a leader, and the closer the match, the more positively that person is typically seen as a leader.",
